    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12432872/comment/12742352",
          "id": "12742352",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=uschindler",
            "name": "uschindler",
            "key": "thetaphi",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956"
            },
            "displayName": "Uwe Schindler",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "Why do you need this?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=uschindler",
            "name": "uschindler",
            "key": "thetaphi",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956"
            },
            "displayName": "Uwe Schindler",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2009-08-12T13:44:38.597+0000",
          "updated": "2009-08-12T13:44:38.597+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12432872/comment/12742354",
          "id": "12742354",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=yseeley%40gmail.com",
            "name": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "key": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Yonik Seeley",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "It makes delegation possible.  Say one wanted to create a new Tokenizer by wrapping an existing Tokenizer or TokenStream.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=yseeley%40gmail.com",
            "name": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "key": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Yonik Seeley",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2009-08-12T13:49:04.828+0000",
          "updated": "2009-08-12T13:49:04.828+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12432872/comment/12742385",
          "id": "12742385",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=uschindler",
            "name": "uschindler",
            "key": "thetaphi",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956"
            },
            "displayName": "Uwe Schindler",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "OK, I was wondering, because TokenFilter is there for this pupose and TokenStream only provides the AttributeSource ctor because the TokenFilter subclass needs this. So one could also simply create a TokenFilter and put it ontop of the Tokenizer to wrap? new TokenFilter(new WrappedTokenizer())  - why need a Tokenizer for that when TokenFilter is made for it?\n\nBut for completeness, this ctor should also get the Reader/CharStream (as all other ctors have the Reader param).",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=uschindler",
            "name": "uschindler",
            "key": "thetaphi",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=thetaphi&avatarId=18956"
            },
            "displayName": "Uwe Schindler",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2009-08-12T14:34:55.851+0000",
          "updated": "2009-08-12T14:34:55.851+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12432872/comment/12742388",
          "id": "12742388",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=yseeley%40gmail.com",
            "name": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "key": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Yonik Seeley",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "bq. But for completeness, this ctor should also get the Reader/CharStream (as all other ctors have the Reader param).\n\nWouldn't tokenizer.reset(reader) serve the same purpose?  I'm not sure why all those different constructors are there.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=yseeley%40gmail.com",
            "name": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "key": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
